/*
 * HS86 Mini 13 TV box (PCB silkscreen RK35X8-EMCP-347-01-V1.0) — Rockchip RK3528.
 *
 * The vendor derived this box from a Hugsun X88PRO DDR4 V10 design and its compatible
 * still says so, so this includes that board and overrides what differs.
 *
 * Checked against the box's own factory device tree, carved from its eMMC: this file
 * compiles to a tree content-identical to that blob plus the changes below. The
 * overrides that follow are the box's own hardware, and carry no reasons because the
 * blob carries none; these are the deliberate departures from it.
 *
 *   model              name the box, keeping the vendor string
 *   reboot-mode        mode-maskrom added, so `reboot maskrom` from the OS reaches the
 *                      BootROM; the factory SPL reads the register on the way up
 *   gpu@ff700000       interrupt-names and clocks in the form mainline lima expects,
 *                      not the vendor Mali blob's
 *   vop@ff840000       esmart_lb_mode 03 -> 02, giving Esmart0 a 4K line buffer
 *   tve@ff880000       rockchip,tvemode added, 01 for NTSC 720x480i. Absent, the driver
 *                      reads an uninitialised value and marks neither CVBS mode preferred
 *   serial@ff9f0000    enabled with uart0m0_xfer, for the ttyS0 console
 *   pwm@ffa90030       remote_support_psci 0 -> 1, so the remote wakes the box
 *   watchdog@ffac0000  enabled, for systemd's RuntimeWatchdogSec
 *   sdmmc              sd-uhs-* dropped; the card is this box's root, and UHS cards can
 *                      fail to re-initialise after a warm reset
 *   wifi-en            disabled; declared active-low, it holds the active-high Wi-Fi
 *                      enable off
 *   sdio-pwrseq        reset-gpios gpio3 B2 active-low and a 200 ms post-power-on delay,
 *                      so the chip is powered with the SDIO host
 *   wireless-wlan      disabled; the vendor rfkill-wlan drives the same enable pin
 *   leds               power/standby labels, renamed from the vendor's pwr-green and
 *                      pwr-red; power gains retain-state-suspended/-shutdown
 *   chosen             dropped; u-boot supplies bootargs, and the vendor string names
 *                      ttyFIQ0
 *   fiq-debugger       disabled; it owns ff9f0000 otherwise
 */
